  "label": "Pivot calculated fields: MPG",
  "group": "Tables",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "Hdr",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "name": "Hdr",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -330,
      "init": {
        "label": "Calculated fields: MPG by vehicle and month",
        "color": "blue",
        "width": 920,
        "height": 150,
        "body": "A pivot's **calculated field** is a LAMBDA wired into a Pivot's Calculated fields row. Its parameters name columns, and every cell hands each one that column's values in its own rows, so `SUM(Miles) / SUM(Gallons)` is miles over gallons for each plate and month, and again for each total.\n\nThat is not the same as working out each fill-up's MPG first and averaging it (the bottom pivot): a short top-up of 60 miles on 3 gallons counts as much as a full tank there, so ABC-123's January reads 25 where the car really did 28. Write the aggregate yourself: `SUM`, `AVERAGE`, `MAX`, any of them, and `@` has no row here."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "Log",
      "type": "FrameInputNode",
      "name": "Log",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "init": {
        "label": "Fuel log",
        "frameText": "[{\"name\": \"Month\", \"type\": \"string\", \"values\": [\"2026-01\", \"2026-01\", \"2026-02\", \"2026-03\", \"2026-03\", \"2026-01\", \"2026-02\", \"2026-02\", \"2026-03\", \"2026-01\", \"2026-02\", \"2026-02\"]}, {\"name\": \"Plate\", \"type\": \"string\", \"values\": [\"ABC-123\", \"ABC-123\", \"ABC-123\", \"ABC-123\", \"ABC-123\", \"XYZ-789\", \"XYZ-789\", \"XYZ-789\", \"XYZ-789\", \"VAN-01\", \"VAN-01\", \"VAN-01\"]}, {\"name\": \"Miles\", \"type\": \"number\", \"values\": [360, 60, 250, 280, 140, 200, 400, 150, 220, 150, 225, 100]}, {\"name\": \"Gallons\", \"type\": \"number\", \"values\": [12, 3, 10, 10, 4, 10, 20, 5, 10, 10, 15, 5]}]"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "MPG",
      "type": "LambdaNode",
      "name": "MPG",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 330,
      "init": {
        "label": "MPG",
        "params": "Miles, Gallons",
        "expr": "SUM(Miles) / SUM(Gallons)"
      }
    },
    {
